WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.418
- Weren't y'all the Women's Dream Team, right?

00:00:01.418 --> 00:00:04.421
- That's sometimes the part that gets sketchy because

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:06.089
here we are for our country,

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:08.216
but we don't really get the recognition in our country.

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:09.384
We don't get the support.

00:00:09.384 --> 00:00:11.261
Our games obviously speak for itself.

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:14.014
So we went 58 and 0.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.016
We played in Russia, we played in China, we played in–

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:16.808
- Whooped all they asses. 

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:19.811
- Cuba, we played in Slovakia, we played you— you name it.

00:00:19.811 --> 00:00:20.603
- [Laughing]

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:31.114
♪♪♪

00:00:33.491 --> 00:00:35.910
- [Master Tesfatsion:] So who we got in the pool hall today?

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.079
Lisa Leslie, what's up with you?

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:40.165
- [Lisa Leslie:] Hey. I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:41.458
How's your pool game?

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:42.792
- Mine's nice, how's yours?

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:46.004
- Man, it’s all good. It's subjective. Where's that little chalk?

00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:47.047
- She about to hustle the hell outta me.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.339
- It’s subjective.
- I don’t even know where it is. 

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:50.633
- I’m actually a lefty. You know that, right?

00:00:52.761 --> 00:00:53.595
- So, Lisa. 

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:56.014
- You are a trailblazer and I appreciate that.

00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:58.349
Of the many things that you do the most,

00:00:58.349 --> 00:01:02.395
what does it take to be a trailblazer, as a Black woman in this country?

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:06.483
- It really is about believing in yourself, learning to love yourself.

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:09.611
And I think for me, listen, I was six foot in the sixth grade.

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:12.447
I wore a size 12 shoe when I was 12 years old.

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:17.035
Now, you look around and you’re like, “Damn.
 That is taller than everybody in this room.”

00:01:17.035 --> 00:01:19.037
Taller than most people at home watching.

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:20.663
And it was different, I was different.

00:01:20.663 --> 00:01:23.291
And so, I think my mom did an amazing job 

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:25.502
of really helping me to understand that.

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:28.880
- In that belief, where did basketball come into the fold?

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.632
- Basketball I feel like is my destiny.

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:33.134
And that was it. I love competition.

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:35.929
Everybody doesn’t like to be competitive and that’s OK.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:39.641
And I think that part was really natural for me. I love to win.

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:43.311
- You talk about all these ambitions and
dreams you had as a kid playing basketball.

00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:45.271
But the WNBA didn’t exist.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.315
So how far did you think you could take basketball?

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:48.733
- Once I got to high school

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:51.528
it was there that I realized you can get a scholarship.

00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:56.491
So that scholarship and me going to college 
to play basketball became the first piece.

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:59.536
The second piece was that I wanted to be 
an Olympian and represent our country. 

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:01.287
Basketball's how I'm gonna travel the world.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:04.749
- So there isn't a professional league, you're at USC, okay?

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:06.042
You enter the Olympics.

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:08.086
Weren't y'all the Women's Dream Team, right? At the time, in '96?

00:02:08.086 --> 00:02:08.670
- Well nobody– 

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.337
- [Laughing]

00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:10.505
- Appreciate the love. 

00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:14.592
That's sometimes the part that it gets sketchy, because again,

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:16.719
here we are for our country,

00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:18.805
but we don't really get the recognition in our country.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.516
We don't get the support the way that we would hope.

00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:25.895
So we went 58 and 0. 58 and 0.

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:27.772
We played in Russia, we played in China, we played in—

00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:28.898
- Whooped all they asses.

00:02:28.898 --> 00:02:31.985
- Cuba, we played in Slovakia, we played you- you name it.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:32.652
- [Laughing]

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.363
- We played everywhere and beat everybody

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:39.784
and it's tough because America's not recognizing any of that.

00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:42.912
You know, nobody sees that, nobody knows about these trips

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:44.831
but it was an amazing time.
- So how was that for y’all then?

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:48.585
The media that you're seeing in Barcelona for the '92 team, it's not there.

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:50.420
How did y'all handle that?

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.257
- They formed the US Olympic team in 1995.

00:02:54.257 --> 00:02:58.428
They created a USA national program where we – 12 of us –

00:02:58.428 --> 00:03:01.723
traveled the world together for the whole year

00:03:01.723 --> 00:03:03.725
playing everybody in their country.

00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:05.435
It was an amazing time in our lives.

00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:09.731
We would never trade any of that, any of our teammates for that experience.

00:03:09.731 --> 00:03:13.651
Representing USA, wearing that red, white, and blue, and kicking butt.

00:03:13.651 --> 00:03:17.155
So having our American flag raised and hearing our anthem

00:03:17.155 --> 00:03:20.700
on podium after podium and having gold medals placed around my neck,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:25.955
that's the highlight of my career because that
was always my ultimate goal and I made it.

00:03:25.955 --> 00:03:26.414
Is it my turn?

00:03:26.414 --> 00:03:27.081
- Hell yeah.

00:03:27.081 --> 00:03:28.416
- I’d like to beat you.

00:03:28.416 --> 00:03:29.792
- You really trying to beat me right now, ain't you?

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:31.377
- Oh, always.

00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:34.881
- So the gap between the Olympics and the inception of the WNBA,

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.132
what are you doing in that meantime?

00:03:36.132 --> 00:03:37.342
- So I was in New York.

00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:40.345
When I get the call- so that's it within that one year, right?

00:03:40.345 --> 00:03:43.181
'96, I'm out, I'm gone.

00:03:43.181 --> 00:03:45.975
And then we get the call about the WNBA and they're like,

00:03:45.975 --> 00:03:47.185
"Oh, it's gonna be in the summer."

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:49.938
 So I'm like, "Okay, cool. It'll be like a summer league, right? 

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:53.650
Like, we wear reversible jerseys, we probably 
play like Long Beach State.” I don’t know.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.945
 By the time it was all put together, we played at the

00:03:56.945 --> 00:04:01.824
Great Western Los Angeles Forum where the Los Angeles Lakers play.

00:04:01.824 --> 00:04:04.577
So like my locker and Kareem's locker is the same locker

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:08.831
and I'm like, “Dude.” I was not ready. You know, I really wasn't.

00:04:08.831 --> 00:04:10.833
[Balls hitting]

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:12.502
You all aggressive with it too.

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:13.461
- [Laughing] 

00:04:13.461 --> 00:04:14.671
- I should hit mine harder.

00:04:14.671 --> 00:04:16.798
- [Laughing] 

00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:20.301
- I was probably, what, seven or eight at the time

00:04:20.301 --> 00:04:22.178
 and I remember the "We Got Next" commercials.

00:04:22.178 --> 00:04:23.346
- See what I’m saying?

00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:24.847
- What do you remember from that shoot with Spike Lee?

00:04:24.847 --> 00:04:27.100
- Now, Spike was awesome because,

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.935
you know, he's an avid basketball fan.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:29.477
- Facts.

00:04:29.477 --> 00:04:32.480
He's New York. Poor Knicks.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.399
Spike is one of those guys who was like,

00:04:34.399 --> 00:04:37.860
"We gotta tell this story because this is really what it is.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.530
Put together, give me your best," which was myself,

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:45.034
Sheryl Swoopes, Dawn Staley. They had men lined up

00:04:45.034 --> 00:04:48.037
cuz they want to be in the commercial but they’re ballers, around the cage.

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:50.123
And so they broke 'em up in four teams.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.667
So there was a guard, you know, a forward and a center.

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:56.296
And we played these men, just like the commercial said, all day.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:59.549
Three-on-three, screening, shooting buckets, blocking shots,

00:04:59.549 --> 00:05:03.261
 like, just really playing these guys. And they filmed all day.

00:05:03.261 --> 00:05:06.389
And like the commercial says, basketball is basketball.

00:05:06.389 --> 00:05:10.351
We didn't win every game, and I will say to this day, we only lost one game.

00:05:10.351 --> 00:05:13.187
So, he says in the commercial, "They didn't win every game,

00:05:13.187 --> 00:05:15.732
but they won enough to say, 'Basketball is basketball.'" 

00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:18.693
And so, that's where the, "Yo, we got next," that was my line.

00:05:19.777 --> 00:05:20.653
You’re kidding. 

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.113
- [Laughing]

00:05:22.113 --> 00:05:23.823
- Just be more aggressive. 

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.534
- It almost feels like, for Black women in the league,

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:28.494
 you gotta be an athlete and like a model.

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.038
Or an athlete and an activist. 

00:05:30.038 --> 00:05:35.084
And it's difficult to just market yourself as a Black
woman that's really really good at the sport.

00:05:35.084 --> 00:05:38.212
Do you see some discrepancies there in terms of how

00:05:38.212 --> 00:05:41.215
white women in the WNBA and how Black women in the WNBA are marketed?

00:05:41.215 --> 00:05:43.801
- This is really being kind of deep but when you think about it

00:05:43.801 --> 00:05:48.014
we watch television and we love white people because we watch shows,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.433
and we've watched shows for many years,

00:05:50.433 --> 00:05:52.727
where we have characters that we love because we're like, 

00:05:52.727 --> 00:05:55.521
"Oh I like Cindy Brady, I like these people."

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:59.150
And I don't look at them based on because 
she's a white girl and I'm a Black girl. 

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.027
I identify with things she's talking about,

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:05.073
things that's going on with her family or maybe what she's wearing, right? 

00:06:05.073 --> 00:06:08.701
So, I don't think we've had that reverse where a lot of white people 

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:12.663
have had the opportunity to see Black people in a way where you would

00:06:12.663 --> 00:06:16.209
like, love, and admire them other than seeing them in sports. 

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:17.168
- I love how you say that too.

00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:19.629
 there's so many of us doing great things on a everyday basis. 

00:06:19.629 --> 00:06:20.129
- Absolutely. 

00:06:20.129 --> 00:06:23.383
-  That should be reflected that people
can find some level of commonality with.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:24.384
- Absolutely.

00:06:25.676 --> 00:06:26.427
- There it is. 

00:06:26.427 --> 00:06:26.886
- Yeah. 

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.429
- [Laughing] 

00:06:28.846 --> 00:06:34.602
♪♪♪

00:06:34.602 --> 00:06:36.813
- So Lisa, let’s see what you can do in the Pop-A-Shot, okay?

00:06:36.813 --> 00:06:38.106
- Alright, let’s do it.
- You got 60 seconds.

00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:40.650
 I’m gonna ask you some questions. Let’s see what you can do, cool?

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:41.234
- Let’s do it. 

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:41.651
- Let’s get it. 

00:06:41.651 --> 00:06:42.026
[Digital beeps from game sounding]

00:06:42.026 --> 00:06:44.153
- 3, 2, 1.

00:06:44.153 --> 00:06:46.864
The one athlete dead or alive you’d wanna play with? 

00:06:46.864 --> 00:06:48.574
- Muhammad Ali. 

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.243
- Who are you listening to before a game?

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.494
- Tupac. 

00:06:51.494 --> 00:06:53.454
- Funniest teammate you’ve ever had?

00:06:53.454 --> 00:06:55.790
- DeLisha [Milton-Jones], by far.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.500
- What’s your signature move?

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.544
- Depends on where the defense is. 

00:06:59.544 --> 00:07:00.169
- What if you’re hittin’ ‘em though?

00:07:00.169 --> 00:07:02.797
- A turnaround off the glass. 

00:07:02.797 --> 00:07:05.591
- Dirtiest opponent you’ve ever faced?

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:06.884
- Latasha Byears, man.

00:07:06.884 --> 00:07:10.179
She’s my teammate. She eventually became my teammate. 

00:07:10.179 --> 00:07:11.722
- Is it a hot dog or a sandwich?

00:07:11.722 --> 00:07:13.015
- Uh. Sandwich. 

00:07:13.015 --> 00:07:14.434
- Favorite pair of kicks you own?

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.018
- Anything by Jordan. 

00:07:16.018 --> 00:07:18.146
- 8 seconds. Gold medal or WNBA Championship?

00:07:18.146 --> 00:07:20.690
- Oh man, always a gold medal. Always. Come on. 

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.900
- Who’s the greatest WNBA player ever?

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.862
- Ever? Including myself? 

00:07:25.862 --> 00:07:27.947
Gotta vote for myself. I got 96 by the way.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:29.866
- You better say yourself.

00:07:29.866 --> 00:07:33.453
- I mean am I in the running or what? You see I got 96, right?

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:35.580
- You killed that thing, Lisa. Yo. 

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.833
- Boom boom. We be old school. Blow it up

00:07:38.833 --> 00:07:39.917
- Thank you for coming to the pool hall.

00:07:39.917 --> 00:07:42.628
It was great to have a legend in the building. Appreciate you. 

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:44.005
- Thanks for having me. This was fun. 

00:07:44.005 --> 00:07:44.547
- You already know. 

